* OPAx197 single-channel functional model for ngspice/KiCad.
* Pin order: IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT
* Two instances represent the two channels of the OPA2197.
*
* This is a linear small-signal model for DC operating points and AC sweeps.
* Datasheet typicals represented: 134 dB open-loop gain (5e6 V/V),
* 10 MHz gain-bandwidth, 5 pA input bias, 100 Megohm / 1.6 pF differential
* and 10 Tohm / 6.4 pF common-mode input impedances, and 1 mA/channel IQ.
* VOS defaults to zero because its datasheet sign varies between parts; set
* VOS explicitly to examine DC offset. ROUT=55 ohm is an approximation.
*
* Output limiting, slew rate, noise, input common-mode range, and output
* current limit are not represented. Do not use this model to predict
* saturation, startup, pulse response, or noise. The earlier nonlinear
* functional model could settle to a false DC operating point in the servo
* loop, producing an incorrect AC linearization.

.subckt OPA1197_FUNC IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT params:
+ AOL=5e6 GBW=10e6 VOS=0 IBIAS=5p IQ=1m
+ ROUT=55 RDIFF=100Meg CDIFF=1.6p RCM=10T CCM=6.4p

RDIFF_IN IN+ IN- {RDIFF}
CDIFF_IN IN+ IN- {CDIFF}
RCM_P IN+ VEE {RCM}
RCM_N IN- VEE {RCM}
CCM_P IN+ VEE {CCM}
CCM_N IN- VEE {CCM}
IB_P IN+ VEE {IBIAS}
IB_N IN- VEE {IBIAS}

* One dominant pole: f_p = GBW/AOL, with unity gain at GBW.
BERR ERR 0 V={V(IN+,IN-)+VOS}
EOL OL 0 ERR 0 {AOL}
RDOM OL DRIVE 1k
CDOM DRIVE 0 {AOL/(2*3.141592653589793*GBW*1k)}
ROUT_OUT DRIVE OUT {ROUT}

IQ_SUPPLY VCC VEE {IQ}
.ends OPA1197_FUNC
